{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Combat clips for Tools/Editor/import_combat_anims.py. See Tools/Data/Anims/README.md for the shopping list and claude-docs/animation.md for the pipeline. Windows (hit, combo, warp_end) are fractions of a clip's length; leave them out to take the role defaults in import_combat_anims.py. Or, per clip, in seconds of the source clip: start_s and end_s keep only that stretch, rate plays it faster (baked into the montage), hit_s and combo_s are the windows; the montage then lands its hit (hit_s[0] - start_s) / rate after the input. Strike numbers come from the fist, foot or bat hand's forward reach per frame, see claude-docs/animation.md. Thug strikes stay at rate 1 here: the game fits them to the telegraph at run time (0.8x to 1.3x, see MeleeComponent's ClipFitMinRate and ClipFitMaxRate).",
  "targets": {
    "uefn": {
      "skeletal_mesh": "/Game/Characters/UEFN_Mannequin/Meshes/SKM_UEFN_Mannequin",
      "ik_rig": "/Game/Characters/UEFN_Mannequin/Animations/Combat/Rigs/IK_Kate_UEFN",
      "chains": "uefn",
      "output": "/Game/Characters/UEFN_Mannequin/Animations/Combat",
      "characters": ["kate", "clint"],
      "root_motion": true
